{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite","id":1208016,"title":"Are there any plans for \"Exalted Lite\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-17T09:31:42-07:00","id":1208016,"title":"Are there any plans for \"Exalted Lite\"","content":"Pretty much as the title says. Are there any plans for a lite version of Exalted? Something that keeps the flavor of Exalted, but who don't really want to deal with a lot of mechanics, book mining, etc.?<br /> <br /> If not, is there any way we can request it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T09:37:24-07:00","id":1208022,"title":"","content":"There are no current plans for that kind of item that i have seen on OPP, nor given their current workload does their seem to be any space for such a creation. I am not a dev nor do I work at OPP, but consider:<br /> <br /> 1) Dragonblooded is currently still in progress<br /> 2) The massive relative success of the DB Kickstarter means the supplement will be more robust than the Solar supplement.<br /> 3) The next pitch they are doing will be for Lunars<br /> 4) Devs hace said in between Lunars and Exigents will be a Realm like supplement. <br /> 5) 4 implies that after Lunars is exigents<br /> 6) The dev team is relatively small<br /> 7) They have expresses desire to make a story teller\u2019s supplement, though I don\u2019t know if this will match your specific expectations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","user":"Saipjas","date":". 04-17-2018, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T09:42:20-07:00","id":1208024,"title":"","content":"I could see fans trying to take Scion's new Storypath system and doing up a light version of Exalted that way, but yeah, I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11967\" data-vbnamecard=\"11967\">Saipjas</a> is right. There's not been anything announced and I wouldn't expect it to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T09:42:29-07:00","id":1208025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208022#post1208022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are no current plans for that kind of item that i have seen on OPP, nor given their current workload does their seem to be any space for such a creation. I am not a dev nor do I work at OPP, but consider:<br /> <br /> 1) Dragonblooded is currently still in progress<br /> 2) The massive relative success of the DB Kickstarter means the supplement will be more robust than the Solar supplement.<br /> 3) The next pitch they are doing will be for Lunars<br /> 4) Devs hace said in between Lunars and Exigents will be a Realm like supplement.<br /> 5) 4 implies that after Lunars is exigents<br /> 6) The dev team is relatively small<br /> 7) They have expresses desire to snake a story teller\u2019s supplement, though I don\u2019t know if this will match your specific expectations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, an Exalted Lite system would be able to be done by a secondary dev team, OPP could do that without changing the main timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T09:48:35-07:00","id":1208031,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar845_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"845\" data-vbnamecard=\"845\">Dragonmystic</a> if you are seeking a new dev team you could theoretically contact RichT to request it. I would however cage your expectations because it would be a significant investiture of resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T09:53:45-07:00","id":1208036,"title":"","content":"I somehow strongly doubt that after all this work the devs are super interested in saying &quot;So if you hate all this work we did we made sure to pay a second team to make the stripped down version.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T10:35:30-07:00","id":1208054,"title":"","content":"Man can you even imagine if they would do such a thing? They would double their playerbase for low effort, because it takes very little effort to de-crunch something down to a more rules lite package. That would be awesome.<br /> <br /> That's also why they would never do it. It'd be a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T10:52:53-07:00","id":1208065,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar255_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"255\" data-vbnamecard=\"255\">ParanoiaCombo</a> it is fine and dandy to say you will \u201cdouble the playerbase\u201d but that assumes several factors. 1) That the decrunch desires of this new group are the same. 2) That they are willing to invest in the line with these decrunched systems. 3) That OPP has the resources to run two concurrent lines for the game development. 4) The costs of doing 3 is less than the gain in profit for a segment of the new group gained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","user":"Saipjas","date":". 04-17-2018, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T10:58:55-07:00","id":1208069,"title":"","content":"There's also the factor of dramatically reducing the complexity of a game is easy, but doing so in such a way that is <i>actually good</i> is not. I can reduce the entirety of D&amp;D down to literally removing every modifier to every roll and even removing rolling in favor of coin flips. That does not automatically improve the game, no matter how much it mechanically simplifies it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T11:11:10-07:00","id":1208073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krata Lightblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208069#post1208069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the factor of dramatically reducing the complexity of a game is easy, but doing so in such a way that is <i>actually good</i> is not. I can reduce the entirety of D&amp;D down to literally removing every modifier to every roll and even removing rolling in favor of coin flips. That does not automatically improve the game, no matter how much it mechanically simplifies it.</div> </div> </div> </div>A PbtA hack of Solars done in 5 hours is better than my entire experience with using EX3's cluttered mess of systems. It's anecdotal but crunch-time is a real factor for people who aren't hobbyists and just want to play a damn game. Lots of those people don't post on forums, either.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T11:14:37-07:00","id":1208074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208024#post1208024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see fans trying to take Scion's new Storypath system and doing up a light version of Exalted that way, but yeah, I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11967\" data-vbnamecard=\"11967\">Saipjas</a> is right. There's not been anything announced and I wouldn't expect it to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that this has anything to do with the topic at hand but man storypath is really not light. It has the slowest, densest dice resolution mechanic I've ever seen that also eats up like all of the game's design space.<br /> <br /> Regarding the topic: I mean, <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?825645-Exalted-What-I-d-Like-in-a-New-Edition&amp;p=21766027#post21766027\" target=\"_blank\">Holden once mentioned he had a plan for something like this</a>, but he was canned so that's never seeing the light of day. Outside of that, I don't know of any plans, and I wouldn't consider it likely to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":77,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","user":"kongurous","date":". 04-17-2018, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T11:15:02-07:00","id":1208075,"title":"","content":"I am of the mind that creating a good, lite system might actually be harder than a sprawling system. Editing times and all that, so I don't have any illusions about that.<br /> <br /> Still, it does capture two types of players with the same lore, refinement, etc. So there is a bit of synergy going on there.<br /> <br /> Has there been any &quot;official&quot; lines that do that? Have two systems for the same universe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T11:15:59-07:00","id":1208078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208065#post1208065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar255_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"255\" data-vbnamecard=\"255\">ParanoiaCombo</a> it is fine and dandy to say you will \u201cdouble the playerbase\u201d but that assumes several factors. 1) That the decrunch desires of this new group are the same. 2) That they are willing to invest in the line with these decrunched systems. 3) That OPP has the resources to run two concurrent lines for the game development. 4) The costs of doing 3 is less than the gain in profit for a segment of the new group gained.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey if you give me 10$ and sandwich I'll write a hack of the game in whatever rules lite system you want. Asking someone to develop a rules lite variant in an existing system is not nearly the hurdle you make it out to be and lots of those systems would welcome partnering with groups like WW/OPP. I mean we can take time to make d20 WW products but not rules lite ones?<br /> <br /> Point 1 is a fair point and I acknowledge that. I'm sympathetic to people though who don't want to be railroaded into playing in a system they don't want. On the other hand I'm more sympathetic to the legion of disappointed people for whom playing Exalted is a choice between a broken system and a working but cumbersome one than I am to the former group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T11:16:34-07:00","id":1208079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208075#post1208075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am of the mind that creating a good, lite system might actually be harder than a sprawling system. Editing times and all that, so I don't have any illusions about that.<br /> <br /> Still, it does capture two types of players with the same lore, refinement, etc. So there is a bit of synergy going on there.<br /> <br /> Has there been any &quot;official&quot; lines that do that? Have two systems for the same universe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadowrun 5th edition and Shadowrun Anarchy come to mind. Anarchy is pretty good, too. It can be done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T11:17:30-07:00","id":1208080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208073#post1208073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A PbtA hack of Solars done in 5 hours is better than my entire experience with using EX3's cluttered mess of systems. It's anecdotal but crunch-time is a real factor for people who aren't hobbyists and just want to play a damn game. Lots of those people don't post on forums, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you are applying your preferences writ large on a segment of the potential game population. You assume because you (subjectively) find that design better that others who want to decrunch the system would agree with you. You could even be right that a portion of the potential new base agrees with you, but it could also run into a situation where you have several competing groups that have different preferences that are mutually exclusive. In this scenario decrunch would not generate sufficient market share to be viable.<br /> <br /> Edit: if you do think that it is a viable idea then I would contact RichT with the pitch. I am not couching that it is impossible, just improbable from a business investment standpoint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","user":"Saipjas","date":". 04-17-2018, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T11:23:55-07:00","id":1208082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208079#post1208079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadowrun 5th edition and Shadowrun Anarchy come to mind. Anarchy is pretty good, too. It can be done.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good to know! I do like that the possibility exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T11:42:45-07:00","id":1208087,"title":"","content":"I don't see how this is possible, honestly.<br /> <br /> You can take the core rules and reduce them down to a minimum level, but even in the core I can see the beginnings of what I expect to balloon out into a bloated mass of fluff and extra mechanics, like every other rules-heavy RPG I've ever seen.<br /> <br /> You would have start with core-lite, have to adapt that fore Solar-lite, then add more &quot;lites&quot; for every other kind of playable character, each of which (I predict) will have its own rules that differ slightly-but-significantly from the core. <br /> <br /> Maybe you can just use the rules from the Quickstart and then wing it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T11:50:21-07:00","id":1208093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208080#post1208080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you are applying your preferences writ large on a segment of the potential game population. You assume because you (subjectively) find that design better that others who want to decrunch the system would agree with you. You could even be right that a portion of the potential new base agrees with you, but it could also run into a situation where you have several competing groups that have different preferences that are mutually exclusive. In this scenario decrunch would not generate sufficient market share to be viable.<br /> <br /> Edit: if you do think that it is a viable idea then I would contact RichT with the pitch. I am not couching that it is impossible, just improbable from a business investment standpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd like to second this because frankly I don't care at all for the hacked down rulesets, I rather like 3e Exalted overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T12:01:05-07:00","id":1208095,"title":"","content":"The thing is, people in the middle crunch spectrum got HOSED by Exalted, which is why this keeps coming up.<br /> <br /> 2E is a broken mess. 2.5 is a bandaid ontop of a sucking maw. 1E has different but persistent problems. 3E *works* and is a perfectly cromulent system but it leaves no room for jesus, if you'll pardon appropriating the conservative expression. What I mean is 3E has so many interlocking systems, a solution in past broken white wolf games (all cWoD games have terrible broken systems) would be to just handwave away stuff. <b>You just can't do that in EX3.</b> Everything is so tightly mechanically interlocked into if-then statements that it's impossible to break away from. If I need to use tools to run the game out of the book,I think that system should probably be in a videogame and not a TTRPG.<br /> <br /> There is no middle way available. There are an awful lot of people in my ear saying &quot;Yeah I like Exalted but EX3 is just so... cumbersome&quot; as a result of that. A broken-bad system would've been better for this group of people who have always played WW games despite their garbage systems. EX3's system is not garbage but it will NOT get out of your way. Thus the gap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T12:01:54-07:00","id":1208096,"title":"","content":"One issue with said parralel development to me is like, what you put in such a book? If you want setting consistency, then it really shouldn't have much to it, or you are in effect laying out two versions of the books to get htings in. And if you try to incorperate both systems into a book, you are just eaitng wordcount. <br /> <br /> Setting consistency is important too since ifyou're not careful, some shifts in one or the other could cause general cannibalization. And due to the difference of systems, if folks buy one over the other, it's not clear if you are actually recouping the costs of in effect running two gamelines as the audience isn't necessairly isomorphic between the two.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T12:03:44-07:00","id":1208097,"title":"","content":"They're doing a storyteller's guide. If a simplified system shows up anywhere it's probably there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T12:15:00-07:00","id":1208098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208096#post1208096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One issue with said parralel development to me is like, what you put in such a book? If you want setting consistency, then it really shouldn't have much to it, or you are in effect laying out two versions of the books to get htings in. And if you try to incorperate both systems into a book, you are just eaitng wordcount.<br /> <br /> Setting consistency is important too since ifyou're not careful, some shifts in one or the other could cause general cannibalization. And due to the difference of systems, if folks buy one over the other, it's not clear if you are actually recouping the costs of in effect running two gamelines as the audience isn't necessairly isomorphic between the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that part is actually easy: think of the Shards book. It had a completely different ruleset in it. Just do a companion pdf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T12:36:53-07:00","id":1208107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208095#post1208095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, people in the middle crunch spectrum got HOSED by Exalted, which is why this keeps coming up.<br /> <br /> 2E is a broken mess. 2.5 is a bandaid ontop of a sucking maw. 1E has different but persistent problems. 3E *works* and is a perfectly cromulent system but it leaves no room for jesus, if you'll pardon appropriating the conservative expression. What I mean is 3E has so many interlocking systems, a solution in past broken white wolf games (all cWoD games have terrible broken systems) would be to just handwave away stuff. <b>You just can't do that in EX3.</b> Everything is so tightly mechanically interlocked into if-then statements that it's impossible to break away from. If I need to use tools to run the game out of the book,I think that system should probably be in a videogame and not a TTRPG.<br /> <br /> There is no middle way available. There are an awful lot of people in my ear saying &quot;Yeah I like Exalted but EX3 is just so... cumbersome&quot; as a result of that. A broken-bad system would've been better for this group of people who have always played WW games despite their garbage systems. EX3's system is not garbage but it will NOT get out of your way. Thus the gap.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hah, Yeah, that medium amount of crunch is just where I fall. Godbound is the true &quot;Lite&quot; alternative to Exalted, but is on the lower end of my crunch level.<br /> <br /> I would argue that 3e isn't actually all that good, but that's design philosophy and I'm not in the mood for a flame war.<sup> (Why on earth is there a JRPG <i>grinding</i> system baked into a TTRPG, crafting? why???)</sup> And I'm trying to channel my frustrations into a more positive, constructive thing--though that is hard.<br /> <br /> Anyway, sidenote over. You are right, trying to pick apart anything of 3e is not easy. Pull a thread and it all has a chain reaction. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T12:47:01-07:00","id":1208116,"title":"","content":"removed ten char","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T12:48:09-07:00","id":1208117,"title":"","content":"@ParanoiaCombo<br /> <br /> I understand where you are coming from, truly I do. And if you think it is as viable as you say it then pitch it. My entire point though is that a lot of what you are saying sounds like anecdata, which could very well be true! But a company who doesn\u2019t have that kind of data on file is not going to move on it and especially if there isn\u2019t someone presenting the work, this is less a game design issue from my standpoint and more a business interest standpoint (though I do feel you are edging into confirming your priors rather than looking at the notion critically). So again, if you feel there is a market share for this and that OPP could stand to make a profit then pitch it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T12:52:49-07:00","id":1208119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208117#post1208117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ParanoiaCombo<br /> <br /> I understand where you are coming from, truly I do. And if you think it is as viable as you say it then pitch it. My entire point though is that a lot of what you are saying sounds like anecdata, which could very well be true! But a company who doesn\u2019t have that kind of data on file is not going to move on it and especially if there isn\u2019t someone presenting the work, this is less a game design issue from my standpoint and more a business interest standpoint (though I do feel you are edging into confirming your priors rather than looking at the notion critically). So again, if you feel there is a market share for this and that OPP could stand to make a profit then pitch it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean, that's kinda what this thread is about. Gauging interest, making some noise, finding out people's opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T12:52:55-07:00","id":1208121,"title":"","content":"Personal axe-grinding in this thread put aside, WW did this in the past, but this was also WW churn out books constantly era. They did D20 versions of some of their games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:04:13-07:00","id":1208125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208119#post1208119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I mean, that's kinda what this thread is about. Gauging interest, making some noise, finding out people's opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your original query was about if this was in the works (which I responded that it wasn\u2019t). Additionally I think I answered your original query about why it wasnt a primary dev concern. I further couched that it was not likely from a business standpoint when you asked about a second line. I would hesitate to use anecdata as actual market research though because confirmation bias is a powerful drug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:11:12-07:00","id":1208128,"title":"","content":"&quot;If not, can we request it?&quot; Was also part of my original post.<br /> <br /> I could also point out that the lack of interest in a lite system is confirmation bias on your part.<br /> <br /> :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:14:13-07:00","id":1208130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208125#post1208125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your original query was about if this was in the works (which I responded that it wasn\u2019t). Additionally I think I answered your original query about why it wasnt a primary dev concern. I further couched that it was not likely from a business standpoint when you asked about a second line. I would hesitate to use anecdata as actual market research though because confirmation bias is a powerful drug.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear you but have you ever heard of a thing called the Pathfinder Beginner Box?<br /> <br /> Pathfinder, for those not in know, is a take on Dungeons and Dragons 3.5 edition, crunch heavy, rules heavy, and cumbersome. Some people love it! It does well in sales (well, until recently). The Beginner Box offers a simplified version of PF rules and every now and again I see a thread pop up on RPG.net &quot;Hey have they ever considered making this the whole game/a version of this?&quot;<br /> <br /> I share that sentiment, obviously.<br /> <br /> I point this out because I strongly believe the demographic who would do well and want these kinds of things are generally not the forum posting hobbyists you get here or in most places online. Heck, the only reason I'm here is because I used to be part of the hobbyist demographic myself, before growing apart from it. I'm not trying to go all &quot;Silent Majority&quot; or anything but I think it's wrong to take these things out of hand. If all you are changing is the rules, and people buy your main books for the fluff, and your KS's make half a million dollars (or a quarter) certainly you could stretch goal or take some cash and pay a dude a couple hundred bucks to write a FATE hack (or whatever system) companion to your game. Then you move your own product and get more people playing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:17:30-07:00","id":1208133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208128#post1208128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;If not, can we request it?&amp;quot; Was also part of my original post.<br /> <br /> I could also point out that the lack of interest in a lite system is confirmation bias on your part.<br /> <br /> :/</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cCan we request\u201d is fundamentally NOT the same thing as pitching a fleshed out product/rule set to a company. Can we request implies that everyone is in agreement (relatively) on what rules they wish to decrunch, and that there is a unified voice. Requesting puts the onus on the developer to create something, where as what I discussed was pitching a concept to paranoiacombo. This puts the onus on the prospective \u201cpitcher\u201d rather than the company who has no established incentive to develop a product. I actually never said I had no interest in such a ruleset (and I challenge you to find a post here that says that from me). Nevertheless, while it may not have salience for me per se it doesn\u2019t mean i can\u2019t be clear eyed about where the onus would need to be for such a project to gain traction. Hence why i even told you on the first page who you should contact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:21:02-07:00","id":1208135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208130#post1208130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hear you but have you ever heard of a thing called the Pathfinder Beginner Box?<br /> <br /> Pathfinder, for those not in know, is a take on Dungeons and Dragons 3.5 edition, crunch heavy, rules heavy, and cumbersome. Some people love it! It does well in sales (well, until recently). The Beginner Box offers a simplified version of PF rules and every now and again I see a thread pop up on RPG.net &amp;quot;Hey have they ever considered making this the whole game/a version of this?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I share that sentiment, obviously.<br /> <br /> I point this out because I strongly believe the demographic who would do well and want these kinds of things are generally not the forum posting hobbyists you get here or in most places online. Heck, the only reason I'm here is because I used to be part of the hobbyist demographic myself, before growing apart from it. I'm not trying to go all &amp;quot;Silent Majority&amp;quot; or anything but I think it's wrong to take these things out of hand. If all you are changing is the rules, and people buy your main books for the fluff, and your KS's make half a million dollars (or a quarter) certainly you could stretch goal or take some cash and pay a dude a couple hundred bucks to write a FATE hack (or whatever system) companion to your game. Then you move your own product and get more people playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, which is why I posted that you should pitch a system to RichT to begin with. My issue is with the concept of \u201crequest\u201d which places the onus on the business and assumes that all people interested in decrunching the system want the same things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:21:58-07:00","id":1208136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208135#post1208135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, which is why I posted that you should pitch a system to RichT to begin with. My issue is with the concept of \u201crequest\u201d which places the onus on the business and assumes that all people interested in decrunching the system want the same things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more interested in the merit of discussion rather than pitching things into an empty void though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:26:35-07:00","id":1208138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208136#post1208136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm more interested in the merit of discussion rather than pitching things into an empty void though</div> </div> </div> </div>See, my view is that a discussion without actionable purpose is fine IF that is understood by all parties. This ties back into my point that you acknowledged that not all decrunchers want the same things. And without a shared mutual understanding at what is meant by \u201clite\u201d the discussion is relatively pointless, as is a general \u201crequest\u201d for which the company has 0 incentive to act on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:26:35-07:00","id":1208139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208136#post1208136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm more interested in the merit of discussion rather than pitching things into an empty void though</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know, right?<br /> <br /> It's also kinda intriguing to deconstruct and reduce Exalted in your mind, trying to figure out what exactly is in the core that makes everything tick. What would a Lite system look like? What is underneath all of the trappings and clothes of Exalted that makes it interesting?<br /> <br /> I dunno, I like that sort of thing; picking it apart and seeing the thematic core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:34:21-07:00","id":1208145,"title":"","content":"Stunt-based improvised charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:34:35-07:00","id":1208146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208138#post1208138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, my view is that a discussion without actionable purpose is fine IF that is understood by all parties. This ties back into my point that you acknowledged that not all decrunchers want the same things. And without a shared mutual understanding at what is meant by \u201clite\u201d the discussion is relatively pointless, as is a general \u201crequest\u201d for which the company has 0 incentive to act on.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify, my position is that OPP wouldn't even consider doing these things, even if they were sufficiently analyzed ideas. I consider pitching to them to be a waste of all of our time. They aren't going to listen.<br /> <br /> What constitutes rules lite or rules medium though? Much more interesting as a topic for fodder, even if not the original OP intent.<br /> <br /> I'd say for Lite the best system you could use would be PbtA. Medium? Much more of a tossup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:36:28-07:00","id":1208147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208016-are-there-any-plans-for-exalted-lite?p=1208139#post1208139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I know, right?<br /> <br /> It's also kinda intriguing to deconstruct and reduce Exalted in your mind, trying to figure out what exactly is in the core that makes everything tick. What would a Lite system look like? What is underneath all of the trappings and clothes of Exalted that makes it interesting?<br /> <br /> I dunno, I like that sort of thing; picking it apart and seeing the thematic core.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn\u2019t what you really asked about though, atleast not explicitly. You asked specific actionable questions. If you wanted to have a theoretical discussion about what a rules lite version of Exalted could be then say so. You asked \u201cis this a thing\u201d and \u201ccan we request a thing\u201d both I feel you have gotten answers to (Not at present for the former, contact RichT for the latter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:40:22-07:00","id":1208152,"title":"","content":"I'm alright with the topic wandering too. This isn't a formalized debate club.<br /> <br /> All these questions do directly relate with me trying to do my conversion. It is interesting to see what people like, so that's helpful for me too.<br /> <br /> Stunt-based charms are good, though I feel like you do need a certain amount of foundation to stand on, or else it becomes a whole &quot;I shot you!&quot; &quot;No you didn't!&quot; problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:46:28-07:00","id":1208155,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar845_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"845\" data-vbnamecard=\"845\">Dragonmystic</a> May I recommend editing the first post and title then so that new comers to the conversation don\u2019t revisit the same discussion previously?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:52:31-07:00","id":1208157,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11967\" data-vbnamecard=\"11967\">Saipjas</a> <br /> <br /> I feel like you're just trying to shut down the thread rather than actively participate.<br /> <br /> Do people want a Lite system? Maybe. Will it happen? Probably not. But it's kinda fun to talk about Exalted, and maybe talk about what might be or might have been? The thread will burn itself out naturally. Until then, just let it be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:58:59-07:00","id":1208163,"title":"","content":"...How does changing the thread to something like \u201cDiscussion: What would a rules lite Exalted look like?\u201d shut down thread?? If anything it would give people who may be interested in discussion the actual thing you want to discuss a chance to take part rather than go to the first page and see you first questions asked and answered, you keep ascribing motives to me that literally the furthest from my mind and I just don\u2019t get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T12:45:57-07:00","id":1208982,"title":"","content":"Does anyone remember the <b>Tomb 5 Corners </b>from 1st Edition? Page 2 was the setting - pages 3-7 was the rules - the rest was the story.<br /> <br /> ...<b>and even more summarized</b>, there was an <b>Exalted &quot;Starter Kit&quot;</b> I <b><i>vaguely </i></b>remember. Less than 2-3 dozen pages, max. <b>Instead of</b> attributes &amp; abilities, they broke it down to 5 stats (one for each archetype... so lets say Combat, Social, Scholar, Crime, Business.......rank them from 1 to 5.... then pick a Caste &amp; Favored (+1 to each). Fighting? Rolling your Combat vs my Combat. Etc.<br /> <br /> ...<b>and even more</b> <b>summarized </b>is probably the <b>Exalted World </b>hack (which is based off Dungeon World, which I think derives from Apocalypse World). It uses Dungeon World's 6 attributes (Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, Charisma, Intelligence, Wisdom) - and treats each Caste as a Class - etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT: BONUS</b><br /> I think I found reference to the 1E Exalted intro kit - and if I get this, the 5 traits used each other for nuance.<br /> <br /> Say 2 martial artists have an equal Fight/Combat/Whatever stat and the result is a tie...<br /> ...<b>then you ask</b> who has the higher Crime stat (ie, dodge, athleticism, awareness, etc).<br /> ...if equal? <b>then you ask</b> who has the higher Social stat (ie, a Zeniths integrity, fortitude, endurance whatever)<br /> ...etc.<br /> <br /> So it wasn't <i>entirely </i>without nuance - it merely set it aside unless characters were equally matched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":". 04-19-2018, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}